From: WF2489T build <wf2489t@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] tools: mkimage: do not store a host pointer in the FIT

fdt_add_size() records a memory reservation at the address of mkimage's
own heap buffer, and replaces an earlier one only if the buffer happens
to sit at the same address again. Both depend on ASLR, so two builds of
the same sources give different FIT images. The reservation means
nothing in a FIT (SPL and U-Boot never read it): store 0 and match on 0,
which always gives the single-entry layout of Rockchip's own images.

--- a/tools/fit_image.c
+++ b/tools/fit_image.c
@@ -40,7 +40,7 @@
 	total = fdt_num_mem_rsv(blob);
 	for (i = 0; i < total; i++) {
 		fdt_get_mem_rsv(blob, i, &addr, &size);
-		if (addr == (uintptr_t)blob) {
+		if (addr == 0) {
 			fdt_del_mem_rsv(blob, i);
 			break;
 		}
@@ -63,7 +63,7 @@
 	fdt_set_totalsize(blob, actualsize);
 
 	/* Add the new reservation */
-	ret = fdt_add_mem_rsv(blob, (uintptr_t)blob, actualsize);
+	ret = fdt_add_mem_rsv(blob, 0, actualsize);
 	if (ret < 0)
 		return ret;
 
